{% comment %}
  Noindex blog tag pages and paginated pages.

  Tag pages (/blogs/the-roll/tagged/SLUG) are auto-generated by Shopify and
  have zero unique content — they duplicate the blog listing and waste crawl
  budget. Google confirmed 1,782 non-indexed pages on RYOP; tag/archive pages
  are the main culprit.

  Paginated pages beyond page 1 get the same treatment: they rarely rank and
  fragment crawl budget.

  PLACEMENT: in Layout > theme.liquid, paste this block INSIDE <head>,
  immediately AFTER the opening <head> tag (before any <meta charset> or
  <meta name="viewport"> is also fine — order doesn't matter for noindex).

  HOW TO CHECK if Impulse already has this:
    In theme.liquid, search for "current_tags". If a <meta name="robots"
    content="noindex"> block already references current_tags, do NOT add
    this file — your theme is already handling it.
    If no such block exists, paste the two lines below into theme.liquid.

  PASTE INTO THEME.LIQUID (inside <head>):
    {%- if current_tags or current_page > 1 -%}
      <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
    {%- endif -%}

  That is the complete fix — no plugin, no app, no JavaScript needed.

  VERIFY: After saving, visit:
    https://www.rollyourownpapers.com/blogs/the-roll/tagged/custom-rolling-paper
  Then View Source and search for "noindex". You should see:
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">

  EXPECTED RESULT IN GSC (4–6 weeks):
  - Tag/archive pages drop from "Crawled – currently not indexed"
  - Indexed page count stabilises and starts rising
  - Crawl budget reclaimed for product and collection pages
{% endcomment %}

{%- if current_tags or current_page > 1 -%}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
{%- endif -%}
